# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE EDITING: when .easignore exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD OF
# .gitignore — not in addition to it. Anything omitted here gets uploaded even
# if git ignores it, so this file has to be self-sufficient.
#
# Why it exists. basemap/data and basemap/out hold ~50 GB of DEM tiles and
# PMTiles archives. They are ignored by basemap/.gitignore, and git honours
# nested ignore files — but EAS walks the filesystem with root-level rules only,
# so it did not see that file and archived the lot. Measured: three abandoned
# tarballs of 42 GB, 39 GB and 16 GB in the EAS temp directory, 204 GB total,
# with a build sitting at "Compressing files" for the better part of an hour.
# The app payload is ~33 MB.

# --- version control and dependencies --------------------------------------
# No trailing slash on .git, and that matters. eas-cli deletes .git from the
# shallow clone only when ignore().add(<this file>).ignores('.git') is true
# (vcs/clients/git.js, makeShallowCopyAsync) — a check that tests the bare
# name, with none of the default rules applied. The pattern `.git/` does not
# match `.git`, so the rule silently does nothing and the whole history ships.
# Measured on Windows: a 32.5 MB upload that should have been ~10 MB, 28 MB of
# it git objects. The trailing slashes elsewhere in this file are harmless —
# exclusion there is decided per file, and every file inside still matches.
.git
node_modules/

# --- the basemap pipeline ---------------------------------------------------
# Source scripts stay (they are small and worth having in the archive for
# reference); the data they produce and consume never ships in an app build.
basemap/data/
basemap/out/
# Per-operator deploy config (names the real host) and the transient copy
# deploy.sh runs from — both hidden by basemap/.gitignore, which EAS never
# reads, so they have to be repeated here.
basemap/config.env
basemap/serve/.deploy-run.sh

# --- scratch and local build inputs -----------------------------------------
# Screenshots, a stray 12 MB PNG, a HEIC photo and a compass zip that nothing
# references, alongside the two files scripts/build-db.mjs reads:
# minfile_occurrences_*.sql and minfile_names.csv. That script is a manual
# local step — no npm script, postinstall or EAS build hook invokes it — and
# its output, artifacts/sgs-minfinder/assets/db/minfile.db, is committed and
# ships on its own. So nothing in here is read during an EAS build. Measured:
# 19.8 MB of a 32 MB archive. Keep the directory in git; the SQL dump and CSV
# are how minfile.db gets rebuilt.
attached_assets/

# --- build output and caches ------------------------------------------------
dist/
.expo/
.expo-shared/
android/
ios/
*.tsbuildinfo
out-tsc/

# --- local env and secrets --------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- editor and OS noise ----------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
